 -- Linus Fischer <leicraft@leicraftmc.de>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:19:05 +0100

leios.theme.plymouth-theme (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make LeiOS the default theme by shipping our own plymouthd.defaults,
    diverting Debian's to /usr/share/plymouth/plymouthd.defaults.distrib,
    instead of editing the file owned by the plymouth package. Theme= in
    /etc/plymouth/plymouthd.conf still takes precedence.
  * On upgrade, restore Debian's theme in the diverted file and remove
    /var/lib/leios.theme.plymouth-theme.
  * Rebuild the initramfs through the update-initramfs trigger.
  * Draw the theme with a Plymouth plugin of its own (leios.so) instead of a
    script: script themes cannot show console output. The box below the
    logo now shows the boot messages a boot without the splash shows
    (kernel messages and systemd status lines, in their colours); before,
    it stayed empty. The package is now architecture-specific.
  * Make the boot message box a rounded translucent box below the logo.
  * Show password and question prompts (e.g. for encrypted disks) in a box
    of their own, and the progress of offline updates below the logo.
  * Make the logo smaller and round its corners like the desktop's.

 -- Linus Fischer <leicraft@leicraftmc.de>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

